  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to occupation of the development hereby approved, a certification by an accredited PV installer confirming that the PV panels with capacity of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-03da6d45-7fff-a439-282d-8f2259838b89&quot;&gt;14 kWp&lt;/span&gt;, has been installed on the roof of the development shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure that the development is adequately sustainable.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Notwithstanding the details shown on the approved drawings, prior to the commencement of the development hereby permitted, a detailed scheme for the internal sound insulation and thermal upgrading of the building shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The scheme shall include a report prepared by a suitably qualified acoustic consultant which demonstrates how the proposed sound insulation will achieve a minimum internal noise level of 30 dB L in all habitable rooms. The approved scheme shall be fully implemented before the occupation of the development and shall thereafter be permanently retained. The development shall not be occupied until a report, prepared by a suitably qualified acoustic consultant, confirming that the approved sound insulation has been installed and meets the required standards, has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;To ensure that future occupiers do not suffer a loss of amenity by reason of noise nuisance and other excess noise.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the occupation of the development hereby approved, details and full specifications of 1 bird boxes, 1 swift bricks/boxes, and 1 bat boxes, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority and shall be maintained for the lifespan of the development. The details should include:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-left: 15px;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 1 swift bricks&amp;nbsp;(same requirements for swift box)&amp;nbsp;incorporated into the design of the development. They should be installed in groups of at least 2, and placed at or close to eaves level of the development hereby approved. They should be placed at least 5m above the ground with a 5m unobstructed flight path, both below and in front of the swift brick. The swift brick should be located facing north, east, or north east (direct sunlight should be avoided) and should not be placed immediately above doors or windows.&amp;nbsp;Where possible, swift bricks should be set flush into the external wall to match adjacent brickwork.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-left: 15px;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 1 bird boxes incorporated into the design of the development, with a variety of box types (including different sized entrance holes) to provide habitat for diverse bird species. The boxes should be installed at or close to the eaves level of the development hereby approved. The boxes should be between 3 and 5 metres from the ground, and there should be a clear flight path without any obstructions below and directly in front of the box. The boxes should be facing north, east or north east (direct sunlight should be avoided), and should not be placed immediately above doors or windows.&amp;nbsp;Boxes located in the same area should not be placed too close together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-left: 15px;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 1 bat boxes incorporated into the design of the development. Boxes should be placed at or close to the eaves level of the development and at least 4m above the ground. The boxes should be placed away from artificial light sources and ideally located near dark tree lines or hedgerows where possible.&amp;nbsp;The boxes should be located facing south, southeast or southwest, and exposed to sun for part of the day.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To support bird and bat populations, including swifts, in Hackney and preserve endangered urban&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;il&quot;&gt;biodiversity&lt;/span&gt;, by providing nesting opportunities, in accordance with Hackney’s Local Plan LP33 policy LP47 which states that all development schemes involving buildings with an eaves height or roof commencement height of 5 metres and above are required to provide nesting boxes for swifts, sparrows, starlings, and/or bats as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the occupation of the development hereby approved, details must be submitted to and approved by the Local Authority to demonstrate at least the consented standards have been met, as set out in the hereby approved Energy Statement (Version 1 by Achieve Green dated 04/04/2025):&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;a) Solar PV panels annual electricity peak generation of 14 kWp&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;b) Array of 15 Solar PV panels&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: In the interest of addressing climate change and securing sustainable and net zero development and construction, in accordance with LP55 of the Hackney Local Plan, SI2 of the London Plan, and Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
